cted return on plan assets"}, {"id": "3ee47bee-1e23-4c65-a3ce-da0743beeb89", "type": "concept", "title": "Actuarial gains/losses"}, {"id": "40b674c0-12a1-4c32-b888-d17961496754", "type": "concept", "title": "Prior service cost and amortization"}], "description": "This subtopic explains funded status and the components of pension expense."}, {"id": "fbbbca34-1dee-4a5d-a32e-dc305ddcee4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recognition and disclosure", "children": [{"id": "c42fea63-d6ef-43d5-afc1-0872124dcf09", "type": "concept", "title": "Funded status on the balance sheet"}, {"id": "753a8639-2869-4dbe-b87c-c20b566ece49", "type": "concept", "title": "OCI and reclassification"}, {"id": "b3d1693d-666e-48eb-b46e-d963bb18c30f", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity and maturity disclosures"}], "description": "Students learn why pension accounting is disclosure-rich and estimate-sensitive."}]}, {"id": "43623c47-203a-4bee-b1d1-6901407a5ad3", "type": "topic", "title": "Leases under ASC 842", "description": "Classify and measure lessee and lessor arrangements, right-of-use assets, lease liabilities, and disclosures.", "children": [{"id": "19842ffd-5223-47e9-b5a2-4c490b4fea75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lease identification and classification", "children": [{"id": "511a2a95-611a-42cf-9529-8e9140ce389e", "type": "concept", "title": "Identified asset and control of use"}, {"id": "ccb10a03-a077-42b0-8926-6b51b42b9a8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Finance versus operating leases"}, {"id": "37dc3c20-4415-46d1-b19f-3114563c2030", "type": "concept", "title": "Short-term lease exemption"}], "description": "Students learn to identify embedded leases and determine classification based on economic control and transfer."}, {"id": "0503a870-e591-4af0-8659-743e99c74751", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lessee accounting", "children": [{"id": "345d2ec9-033c-4724-95da-2c1b265b0b0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Initial measurement"}, {"id": "66541707-8603-47af-a95c-07423a636106", "type": "concept", "title": "Subsequent measurement"}, {"id": "fab5b406-8828-438b-bd54-8a3d79fd7a08", "type": "concept", "title": "Remeasurement, modifications, and impairment"}], "description": "This subtopic covers right-of-use assets, lease liabilities, and income statement patterns."}, {"id": "093f4ee4-5c7d-4487-83f0-dc888d5337e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lessor accounting and disclosures", "children": [{"id": "d13a4a07-81ce-4809-a280-2320bd94bcc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Sales-type, direct financing, and operating leases"}, {"id": "440e1a22-b31f-4b8f-887c-51b0a1f20d5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Residual value and collectibility"}, {"id": "8064b190-28c1-4462-911b-23ec17be08f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Maturity analyses and weighted-average assumptions"}], "description": "Students learn the other side of lease contracts and the disclosures users need."}]}, {"id": "282392f9-78e2-4f39-b6a6-6146b848a197", "type": "topic", "title": "Accounting changes, estimates, and error corrections", "description": "Distinguish changes in principle, estimate, entity, and errors; apply retrospective and prospective treatment.", "children": [{"id": "95a7db62-0fe9-4b79-b5e3-63c7c7da7aaf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Types of accounting changes", "children": [{"id": "d761accc-357a-4d08-865e-997aa7d5fb3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Change in accounting principle"}, {"id": "0f0370e8-b3b8-45d3-8d22-a4129608e425", "type": "concept", "title": "Change in accounting estimate"}, {"id": "794ec6be-6b07-426d-8f83-37c7b7e6f9ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Change in reporting entity"}], "description": "Students learn to classify changes correctly before deciding how to report them."}, {"id": "262b7454-5eae-426f-bb0d-ddf57d1f3e0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Retrospective and prospective treatment", "children": [{"id": "63afaeaa-e28d-44a7-9097-f835787352b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Retrospective application"}, {"id": "f2f70d61-ca49-420a-8937-d5c9220a5bd5", "type": "concept", "title": "Prospective treatment"}, {"id": "a5924d1f-edf5-49ad-ba15-23f9f5e36c6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cumulative-effect adjustments"}], "description": "This subtopic explains when prior periods are restated and when future periods absorb the change."}, {"id": "65649149-723f-4627-894a-0f6e2f77b9f0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Error correction and disclosure", "children": [{"id": "0acf82fe-5cf0-45f1-bbf0-4112a4a3581e", "type": "concept", "title": "Prior-period adjustments"}, {"id": "e01c599e-12c2-4c44-8317-e703e37e374b", "type": "concept", "title": "Restatement triggers"}, {"id": "2d45c4ac-1c34-43b3-b44f-36436908cd70", "type": "concept", "title": "Materiality, internal controls, and disclosure requirements"}], "description": "Students learn how material errors are corrected and communicated."}]}, {"id": "a49d9063-a334-4f79-8f5d-136864755843", "type": "topic", "title": "Statement of cash flows: advanced topics", "description": "Prepare complex cash flow statements involving noncash transactions, indirect-method adjustments, and classification judgment.", "children": [{"id": "6451a5a3-6bfb-42d1-9e12-1899396dbe0b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Classification judgment", "children": [{"id": "86f63ebf-209e-412e-afcf-e5b8b70496a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Operating, investing, and financing sections"}, {"id": "375c9b6a-961d-4002-a651-fc69952b7a5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest, taxes, dividends, and restricted cash"}, {"id": "41f93f60-9ca2-448b-8cea-cbda81518a9f", "type": "concept", "title": "GAAP and IFRS comparison points"}], "description": "Students learn to classify cash flows consistently and understand where reporting choices arise."}, {"id": "bd1463c4-e666-405a-a5e9-c7f9b7ef9402", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Indirect method complications", "children": [{"id": "6d442a95-d42e-4918-97ee-cda399f1dcd5", "type": "concept", "title": "Deferred taxes, pensions, leases, and stock compensation"}, {"id": "146e6584-2bb8-47a7-8134-fe69aab842cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Gains/losses and noncash expenses"}, {"id": "50bc0e8b-47ee-4966-9fef-05a0affa6c94", "type": "concept", "title": "Working capital changes and unusual items"}], "description": "This subtopic connects accrual accounting topics back to operating cash flow."}, {"id": "f1a0300b-99a3-48f6-9baf-918920da0d19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Noncash and supplemental disclosures", "children": [{"id": "d2c288f8-a9fd-4703-9146-2befca76605d", "type": "concept", "title": "Noncash investing and financing activities"}, {"id": "4a7fb346-9343-4b71-9c6a-eb141508ec95", "type": "concept", "title": "Lease additions and debt conversions"}, {"id": "3770e2b4-90c6-4465-9d14-ae61e5ff6392", "type": "concept", "title": "Cash paid for interest and taxes"}], "description": "Students learn how major transactions bypass cash flow sections while still mattering to users."}]}, {"id": "14fc31d8-0b89-45e4-8475-7afd70dd98eb", "type": "topic", "title": "Disclosure, filing analysis, and integrative reporting cases", "description": "Use real filings to connect technical accounting to notes, MD&A, materiality, comparability, and user decision-making.", "children": [{"id": "553761a9-b3af-42ed-a6c2-559156db56e8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Footnote analysis", "children": [{"id": "8c4a0728-e27f-448e-abe8-79b1e72e038c", "type": "concept", "title": "Accounting policies"}, {"id": "2dea0a61-6673-4b8e-823d-bf7215999b16", "type": "concept", "title": "Critical estimates"}, {"id": "02755990-ff23-48ff-9655-3660b3079b84", "type": "concept", "title": "Revenue, lease, tax, pension, debt, and investment notes"}], "description": "Students learn to use notes as the bridge between technical accounting and economic interpretation."}, {"id": "d5fe1020-e45b-4550-8e2b-76e259578d99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparability and quality of reporting", "children": [{"id": "681fdd6c-0173-487d-9308-84f36f942477", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy choices and estimates"}, {"id": "8b83f3f1-2338-4b83-bbd4-69